    <bpmn:process id="W_W3447" name="W3447. Strategic Account Loss &amp; Competitive-Displacement Analysis" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Lost strategic account or major deal
Frequency: Event-driven + quarterly portfolio
Volume: All material losses
Owner: Head of Strategic Accounts
Participants: Head of Strategic Accounts, Account Manager, Competitive Intel (links to VS-57/VS-33.3), Merchandising (links to VS-01), Service (links to VS-12)
Source: workflow W3447 — Strategic Account Loss &amp; Competitive-Displacement Analysis</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3447_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3447_Lane1" name="Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3447_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3447_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3447_Lane2" name="Head of Strategic Accounts">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3447_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3447_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3447_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3447_Start4" name="Lost strategic account or major deal">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3447_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3447_Task5" name="Account Manager conduct the loss review: root cause (price links to VS-01.2…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Account Manager conduct the loss review: root cause (price links to VS-01.2, product/assortment links to VS-01, service links to VS-12, relationship links to W3429, credit links to VS-68, competitor offer links to VS-57), decision process, and what would have changed the outcome; document findings
Responsible (R): Account Manager / CI
Accountable (A): Head of Strategic Accounts
Duration: Per loss</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3447_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3447_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3447_Task6" name="Head of Strategic Accounts/CI aggregate loss patterns across the portfolio…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Head of Strategic Accounts/CI aggregate loss patterns across the portfolio: recurring root causes, competitor tactics, segment/category concentration, and disintermediation signals (e.g., customer direct-import links to VS-87); identify systemic issues
Responsible (R): Head of Strategic Accounts / CI
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3447_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3447_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3447_Task7" name="Head of Strategic Accounts drive systemic remediation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Head of Strategic Accounts drive systemic remediation: pricing/assortment/service fixes (links to VS-01/VS-12), competitive response (links to VS-57/W329), training (links to VS-43.3/VS-19.4), and process improvement; report loss analysis and remediation to executives (links to VS-33.2) and feed to the KAP cycle (W3427)
Responsible (R): Head of Strategic Accounts
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management / COO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3447_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3447_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3447_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3447_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-552 (ensure controlled execution — Account Profitability, Retention &amp; Strategic Analytics (PA-107.3).) | - operational: rigorous loss review; operational: systemic remediation tracking and exec reporting
Owner: Head of Strategic Accounts</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
